# Equality as an indexed family: `equal a / head / read x / head / read y` is the type of proofs that the two values
# `x` and `y` of type `a` are the same, and its one constructor `refl` only builds `equal a c c`.
#
# `x` and `y` are VALUE INDICES (`head x, like a`), and every use writes them as `head` children. Until 2026-10-02
# they were fields (`link x, like a`) and uses wrote `like equal a x y`, which the checker read as `equal a` with two
# extra type arguments it quietly dropped. So `equal a x y` and `equal a u v` were the same type, and the kernel
# proved "any x equals any y" by `make equal/refl` (proof-by-default-0031). Every proof under proof/equal/ was
# rewritten against this, and test/check/soundness.ts holds the false ones refused.
form equal
  head a
  head x, like a
  head y, like a
  case refl
    link c, like a
    head
      read c
    head
      read c
